 34MG c  2014Mi09: a 63-MeV/nucleon {+48}Ca primary beam was accelerated by the 
 34MG2c  RIKEN RFQ-RILAC-CSM-RRC accelerator complex. Secondary beams containing
 34MG3c  {+34}Mg were produced by fragmentation of the primary beam on {+181}Ta 
 34MG4c  and enriched {+64}Ni targets, separated by the RIPS fragment separator,
 34MG5c  and bombarded the liquid hydrogen secondary target at 51.1 MeV/nucleon.
 34MG6c  The scattered particles were analyzed by the TOMBEE spectrometer and   
 34MG7c  detected using a |DE-E telescope of a silicon detector and a NaI(Tl)   
 34MG8c  detector. The |g rays from the excited states populated by inelastic   
 34MG9c  scattering were detected by the DALI2 array of 160 NaI(Tl) detectors.  
 34MGAc  Measured E|g with Doppler correction, |g yields, ({+34}Mg)|g-coin, and 
 34MGBc  |g|g-coin. Deduced levels, cross sections for population of excited    
 34MGCc  states, deformation lengths, and deformation parameters |b{-2}.        
 34MGDc  Compared with SDPF-M shell-model calculations.                         
 34MG c  2006El03: a 94-MeV/nucleon {+40}Ar primary beam was transported to a   
 34MG2c  {+181}Ta primary target. The secondary beams of {+30}Na, {+31}Na, and  
 34MG3c  {+34}Mg were separated by the RIPS fragment separator and bombarded a  
 34MG4c  liquid hydrogen target at a mean energy of 50 MeV/nucleon. The reaction
 34MG5c  products were detected and identified by a parallel-plate avalanche    
 34MG6c  counter (PPAC) and a silicon detector telescope. The deexciting |g rays
 34MG7c  emitted by the inelastically scattered nuclei were detected by the     
 34MG8c  DALI2 setup consisting of 146 NaI(Tl) detectors. Deduced mass          
 34MG9c  deformation and neutron deformation parameters.                        
